{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794757792,"nonce":"Xag+snsah1Vzy/DpyqVsJG7Sc+k=","message":"Two changes landed locally (not pushed): a41a4460 (rows find a bound node's group by id) and 622804fe (the atlas takes groups cut by the viewport).\n\nWhat the measurement found. A grid of small bordered cards, each fading by a motion binding (animation_paths: what_a_frame_costs_with_many_faded_cards, headless, median ms a frame including the render and read-back every path pays; the same grid moving on rows costs about 2 ms):\n\n- before: every frame a full paint on every path; 10, 40 and 140 cards on rows cost 6.1, 9.3 and 23.0 ms.\n- a41a4460: the planner could not tell the groups apart (cards inside wrappers all have position 0,0 and one size, so find_group matched many and declined); with an id, rows apply on every frame (0 of 57 painted in full). 140 cards: 12.3 ms.\n- 622804fe: the cards in the left column and top row stuck out of the viewport by their border's outset, were \"cut\", and each ended the run of groups, so a frame took about 15 atlases of nine cards plus a group of its own for each cut card, a few render passes each. They are in the atlas now. 140 cards: 2.8 ms (2.7 to 2.9 across runs), with or without a label.\n\nHeld to the full paint: \"motion fade, equal cards\" is in the scenes and in ON_ROWS, 0 differing pixels at 2 levels; the atlas test now puts groups cut at the right, left and top edges in one atlas and compares them with drawing each alone, within 1 level at 1 and 4 samples. blinc_layout, blinc_recorder, blinc_app, blinc_animation and blinc_gpu under nextest: the failures that remain are the two stateful tests and, on this Mac, the HLSL check (needs dxc), a particle golden and a tbc canary (see the new issue).\n\nNot done, so this stays open: a group that is one of a kind or over 512 px a side, one that holds an image, a path, a mesh or a clip frame, and the idea of keeping the rendered atlas between frames when only the opacity changed. After the two changes a plain group fade costs about what a moving card does in this harness, so that last item has no number behind it yet; measure on the Pixel before building it. Phones and windows were not run.","files":null}]}